# Videos page

## Finish line

Pinned 2026-09-29 in a grilling session with Vojta, then reshaped the same day
mid-build (see the ledger). Ships as **one PR**.

- `/videos` is a hub page listing **every video the viewer can watch**, one
  card per video: free posts and free-tier lessons for everyone, plus every
  lesson a course they own opens. No cohort, workshop or tutorial cards.
- Cards are the homepage posts-grid card (`ResourceCard`) with YouTube-style
  inline playback on hover (`inlinePlayback`): the Mux HLS stream with its
  subtitles on, muted until the viewer unmutes (speaker and CC buttons on the
  thumbnail, remembered across cards and visits), a progress bar, and a click
  that opens the video where the preview got to (`?t=`). Runtime on the
  thumbnail when known, ✓ Watched, and for lessons "From <course>" plus a
  `Free preview` badge when it is a free lesson from a course the viewer does
  not own. No Post/Article labels.
- The grid runs on Typesense with index fields derived from resource relations,
  never hand-set (`src/lib/video-facts.ts`): `has_video`, `free`, `course_ids`,
  `duration_seconds`, `container_title`, `mux_playback_id`, `thumbnail_time`.
- Controls: search, `Newest · Popular`, `Hide watched` (once something is
  watched), and `All · My courses` (only for someone who owns a course), all
  URL-synced. Preview sound and captions live on the cards, not the toolbar.
- The derived fields self-heal: an hourly Inngest reconcile
  (`typesense-video-facts-reconcile`, :17 past each hour) recomputes them,
  updates only changed docs, and rebuilds through the save path (up to 100 a
  run) any watchable video missing from the index or with drifted
  `visibility` / `state`.

## Vocabulary

- **video** — a resource that is a video itself: a post, lesson, exercise, tip
  or talk with a ready Mux `videoResource`. Solutions ride on their exercise and
  are not listed.
- **free** — watchable without a purchase: posts, tips and talks anywhere; a
  lesson whose join row (or its section's) in an open module carries
  `metadata.tier === 'free'`.
- **course_ids** — every course that currently opens a video: its open
  workshops and the cohorts or lists around them. "Videos from courses you own"
  is `course_ids ∩ ownedIds`, so the filter carries a handful of course ids
  rather than hundreds of lesson ids.
- **open** — a workshop is open when it is `published` and its `startsAt` has
  passed (`isWorkshopAvailable`). Cohort days are published ahead and open on
  schedule; the hourly reconcile moves a lesson into its courses within the hour.
- **free preview** — a free lesson shown to someone who does not own its course.

## Notes

- Content shape on 2026-09-29 (prod DB): 63 posts and 411 lessons with a ready
  video; 23 lessons free-tier (5 in the Personal Assistant cohort's "Before We
  Start", 18 in `ai-sdk-v6-crash-course`'s two free sections); 317 lessons
  opened by some course. No two lessons share a Mux playback id, so owners of
  several cohort runs see no duplicates.
- **Lesson state gates nothing inside a course.** The live, sold AI Coding
  Crash Course is 60 `draft` lessons. Workshop state and schedule gate; post
  state gates. So the filter never requires a lesson to be published — `free`
  and `course_ids` already require an open course.
- Tier lives on the `ContentResourceResource` join (`metadata.tier`), not on the
  lesson. Tier changes go through the CMS workshop reorder, which never
  reindexes — hence the reconcile.
- 89 course lessons had never been indexed on 2026-09-29; the first production
  reconcile rebuilds them.
- Runtimes are mostly unknown: 17 of 55 published video posts and 0 of 147
  published video lessons had a duration (course-sync stamps it; the old Mux
  path never did). Runtime badges show only when known.
- The prod collection has a `.*` auto field, so the new fields need no schema
  migration; they are declared in `scripts/typesense-migrate.mts` for rebuilds.
  `course_ids` is written as `null`, never `[]`: auto-typing cannot type an
  empty array. Until the first reconcile writes `has_video`, the page's filter
  errors — run the reconcile before the page ships.
- `ck_subscriber` is httpOnly, so `videos.viewerStatus` always runs; anonymous
  visitors get the empty status without a DB read. The cookie may reveal what a
  viewer watched (as module progress already does) but never what they own.
- Hover previews and sound: hovering is not a user gesture, so browsers refuse
  unmuted autoplay until the visitor has clicked or typed on the page.
  MuxPlayer's `autoPlay="any"` tries with sound and falls back to muted; the
  speaker button's own click is the gesture that makes sound work. Subtitles
  exist only in the HLS stream (Mux text tracks), not in the `low.mp4` the
  homepage preview loops, so inline playback uses HLS. `disableTracking` keeps
  hover previews out of Mux Data views.
- A playing video is its own compositing layer and escapes a rounded
  `overflow-hidden` clip (square corners, a light edge). The thumbnail clips
  with `clip-path: inset(0 round 10px)`. The player stays invisible until
  `playing` and fades in over the still, so there is never an empty box.
- Both players read `?t=<seconds>` (`PostPlayer`, and `AuthedVideoPlayer`
  where it beats the saved resume position). A card only adds `t` after 3+
  seconds of preview, so an untouched lesson still resumes where the viewer
  left it.
- Matt's YouTube uploads and live streams are not content resources and are not
  on this page.
- Gotchas carried from [[typesense-index-paths]]: both index paths call the
  same derivation; the bulk script does not run under plain `tsx`; check which
  collection `.env` targets before any write.

## Decision ledger

Settled 2026-09-29 by Vojta in the grilling session:

1. ~~Card unit — standalone videos as cards; a container is one card.~~
   Superseded by 14.
2. ~~Container card links out to the container page.~~ Superseded by 14.
3. Free = watchable without buying (see Vocabulary).
4. ~~Paid unit is the cohort.~~ Superseded by 14.
5. Data source is Typesense, with facts derived from relations by one shared
   function both index paths call.
6. Freshness: derive at save time + hourly reconcile. Rejected: hooking every
   relation-write path (the CMS kit is shared with three other apps and a miss
   is silent).
7. v1 personalization is card status only. "Continue watching" is the next
   layer and needs `PostPlayer` to save playback position first.
8. Viewer status loads in one tRPC query after the session resolves; Hide
   watched goes to Typesense as `id:!=[…]`.
9. ~~Every cohort with video shows to everyone.~~ Superseded by 14.
10. ~~Cards reuse the `/posts` hit card.~~ Superseded by 15.
11. No type or topic facets in v1.
12. Hub page via `HUB_PREFIXES`, linked under **Explore** in the CMS
    `hub-sidebar` page and `hub-sidebar-fallback.ts`. Primary nav unchanged.
13. One PR. Verify indexed counts against the DB before merge.

Mid-build calls (Vojta, 2026-09-29):

14. **Show every video the viewer has access to, one card per video.**
    Containers on the grid read as weird. Anonymous viewers see free videos;
    owners also see their courses' lessons. Replaces the All/Free/Owned control
    with `All · My courses`.
15. Cards are the homepage posts-grid card with hover autoplay. `ResourceCard`
    gained optional `badges` / `overlay` / `meta` slots so both pages share it.
16. No Post/Article labels: on this page everything is a video.
17. "More like YouTube": hover previews play with subtitles and, once unmuted,
    sound; controls sit on the thumbnail; the homepage keeps its silent loop.
18. Clicking a card after watching its preview opens the video at that point.

Verified 2026-09-29 against a clone of `content_production`
(`content_vojta_videos_test`): anonymous = 75 videos (53 posts, 22 free
lessons); an owner of four cohorts plus AI SDK v6 = 272 (219 lessons before the
89 missing ones are indexed); a second reconcile pass writes 0 docs.

